{"base_rate":0.17269076305220885,"brier":0.1125334672021419,"bss":0.21232925039512307,"bss_hi":0.31861012796732463,"bss_lo":0.0649077187300723,"chart":{"base":[211.3,187.8],"fp":[236.2,103.8],"lead":"62,228.7 272,185.3 482,160.3 692,111.4","note":{"base":"skill 0.21 — higher than 29% of cities","fp":"low end +1pp, high end +31pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 25% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 2%; promised 87% → rained 56%"},"rel":"66.1,455.3 252.4,368.7 611.6,224.1"},"country":"PK","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08908969210174031,"ess":386.1965404428999,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Lahore</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Lahore rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (98%), believe about\n<b>69%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>2%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 747 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 1.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.21, ranked 153 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(90&ndash;184) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>2%</b></td><td class='num'>370</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>19%</td><td class='num'><b>17%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>42%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>76%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>98%</td><td class='num'><b>69%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Lahore</b> <span class=\"muted\">Pakistan</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;17% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 17% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.21</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>90&ndash;184\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>747 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Lahore &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Lahore\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 71.64763157894737,348.4736842105263 123.55896103896104,282.72727272727275 208.06729729729733,185.24324324324323 328.2672,71.38666666666666 405.3448,18.0 405.3448,37.413333333333355 328.2672,139.33333333333334 208.06729729729733,263.94594594594594 123.55896103896104,344.1818181818182 71.64763157894737,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"319.140562248996\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"319.140562248996\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,376.0972972972973 71.64763157894737,358.0526315789474 123.55896103896104,320.54545454545456 208.06729729729733,278.7027027027027 328.2672,226.69333333333333 405.3448,129.62666666666667\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 2% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 370 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"376.0972972972973\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.64763157894737\" cy=\"358.0526315789474\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 19%&amp;#10;It rained 17% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"123.55896103896104\" cy=\"320.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 42%&amp;#10;It rained 28% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"208.06729729729733\" cy=\"278.7027027027027\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 76%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"328.2672\" cy=\"226.69333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 98%&amp;#10;It rained 69% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"405.3448\" cy=\"129.62666666666667\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(17%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Lahore the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.39) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.06).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>179</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>-0.061</td><td class='num'>19.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>213</td><td class='num'>16%</td><td class='num'>0.212</td><td class='num'>6.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'>0.331</td><td class='num'>5.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>181</td><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'>0.388</td><td class='num'>5.6%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":31.558,"lon":74.35071,"n":747,"n_cities":216,"name":"Lahore","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":370,"obs":0.016216216216216217,"sig":true},{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.03855263157894737,"n":76,"obs":0.06578947368421052,"sig":false},{"hi":0.30200000000000043,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.1851948051948052,"n":77,"obs":0.16883116883116883,"sig":false},{"hi":0.5880000000000006,"lo":0.30200000000000043,"mean":0.423918918918919,"n":74,"obs":0.28378378378378377,"sig":true},{"hi":0.9079999999999996,"lo":0.5880000000000006,"mean":0.7634666666666666,"n":75,"obs":0.4266666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.9079999999999996,"mean":0.9812000000000001,"n":75,"obs":0.6933333333333334,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.9,"provisional":false,"rank":153,"rank_hi":184.0,"rank_lo":90.0,"reliability":0.02188769267330396,"resolution":0.04820624839747621,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"lahore","station":"","timezone":"Asia/Karachi"}